{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-93999" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}\\,∗\\, & -\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ \\,∗\\, & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ shown above. Given that $A=PD{P}^{T}$ is an orthogonal diagonalization of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ for some diagonal matrix $D,$ which of the following could be the first column of the matrix $P?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075254/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c713f835cfca54045907739e077837151d35744ed142660e7e682b56fb413e0"} {"question" "q-93999" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a matrix $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable if there exists an orthogonal matrix $P$ such that\n\n$$\nA=PD{P}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a diagonal matrix.\n\nMoreover, a matrix $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable if and only if it is symmetric.\n\nSince  $A=PD{P}^{T}$ is an orthogonal diagonalization of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A,$ the matrix $P$ must be a $2\\times 2$ orthogonal matrix. This means that \n\n- the first column must be orthogonal to the second column, and\n\n- the norm of the first column must be equal to $1.$\n\nAmong the given options, only the vector $[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}]$ has both properties." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075254/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c713f835cfca54045907739e077837151d35744ed142660e7e682b56fb413e0"} {"question" "q-93999" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075254/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d3a446f9562ec0de41761947788297a161d1086c70da4370254